{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development does not present a high-quality of design. Its large scale does not appear subordinate when viewed in relation to the host first floor flat. The principle of introducing a self-contained outbuilding of&nbsp;primary residential use within the garden setting is not supported, and its use does not present an established ancillary relation to the host first floor flat. The proposal therefore represents an&nbsp;inappropriate and uncharacteristic residential form. As such, the proposal is contrary to:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC, 2023); Policies D1 and D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);&nbsp;Policy CP3 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework Core Strategy (July 2010);Policies BP8 and BP11 of the LDF Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011);Policies SP2,&nbsp; SP4, DMD1 and DMD6 of the Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Consultation Version, October 2020); Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
  ],
